    "observations": [
      "The orchestrator copied each packet and report from the track working folder under tmp/agent-runs/ to the manifest paths after the track finished, and derived each track start from the creation time of that folder.",
      "The report schema of prompts/prism-agent-reviewer-v1.4.md prescribes a middle-dot separator that the operator's style rules exclude, so tracks followed one or the other. No coding depends on it.",
      "The prepared manifest listed the records D2EGAVKZ, Y6SAPNT2 as aliases although the registry binds them to another Version of the same Work. The orchestrator removed them from assignment.papers[].record_ids before integration, so they receive no coding from this run. The coding packets and the AI Agent Review cover the representative papers only and are unaffected.",
      "The orchestrator normalised agent-written CRLF line endings to LF in ar2-coding.json before commit, because the repository checks text out with LF, and recomputed the dependent hashes in this manifest and the packet hashes listed in ai-agent-review.json. Content is otherwise unchanged. The PRISM track ar2 and its projection were rebuilt from the normalised packet, since the track binds the packet hash."
    ]
